    "question_text": "Explain the difference between a list and a generator in Python, and describe a situation where a generator is the better choice.",
    "question_type": "essay",
    "complexity": "high",
    "options": [],
    "correct_answer": "A list stores all of its elements in memory and supports indexing and repeated iteration. A generator produces values lazily, one at a time, keeping only its state in memory, and can be consumed once. Generators are preferable for large or unbounded sequences, streaming data or pipelines (for example reading a multi-GB log file line by line) because they use constant memory.",
    "image_key": null,
    "created_by": {
      "$oid": "6b06f47cc37c2b5d330a522f"
    },
    "created_at": {
      "$date": "2026-10-17T17:00:27Z"
    },
    "updated_at": {
      "$date": "2026-10-17T17:00:27Z"
    }
  },
